p"},{"type":"text","value":" executions create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.step"},{"type":"text","value":" spans. Replayed\nsteps do not create fresh step execution spans because no user step code ran."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"privacy-defaults","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Privacy defaults"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workflow tracing intentionally does not record workflow input, workflow output,\nsignal payloads, step results, or arbitrary step metadata as attributes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in attributes are stable identifiers and counts:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.workflow_id"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.workflow_version"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.run_id"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.operation"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.result_kind"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.step_id"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.signal_name"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.schedule_id"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.bucket_id"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.lease_owner"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.event_count"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack.workflow.events_truncated"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want to add safe application attributes, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"telemetry.attributes"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"telemetry.mapStepMeta"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configure-tracing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure tracing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Initialize OpenTelemetry in your app before Workflow code runs. Then create the\nruntime normally:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineWorkflowRuntime } from '@tanstack/workflow-runtime'\n\nexport const workflowRuntime = defineWorkflowRuntime({\n  store,\n  workflows,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workflow uses the global OpenTelemetry tracer provider by default."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To customize Workflow tracing:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const workflowRuntime = defineWorkflowRuntime({\n  store,\n  workflows,\n  telemetry: {\n    spanNamePrefix: 'tanstack.workflow',\n    attributes: ({ workflowId }) => ({\n      'app.workflow_id': workflowId ?? 'unknown',\n    }),\n    mapStepMeta: (meta) => ({\n      'app.step_name': String(meta.name),\n    }),\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mapStepMeta"},{"type":"text","value":" for metadata you know is safe to export. Workflow does\nnot export step metadata by default."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disable tracing for a runtime:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const workflowRuntime = defineWorkflowRuntime({\n  store,\n  workflows,\n  telemetry: false,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"deployment-notes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deployment notes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Host adapters do not need separate tracing configuration. Netlify, Vercel,\nCloudflare, and Railway helpers call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runtime.sweep()"},{"type":"text","value":", so they inherit the\nruntime spans automatically."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For serverless platforms, initialize the OpenTelemetry SDK in the platform's\nrecommended instrumentation entrypoint. Workflow only emits spans through the\nOpenTelemetry API; exporter flushing and process lifecycle are app concerns."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"observability","text":"Observability","level":1},{"id":"what-is-traced","text":"What is traced","level":2},{"id":"privacy-defaults","text":"Privacy defaults","level":2},{"id":"configure-tracing","text":"Configure tracing","level":2},{"id":"deployment-notes","text":"Deployment notes","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n# Observability\n\nTanStack Workflow emits OpenTelemetry traces from the runtime and core engine.\nThe packages depend only on `@opentelemetry/api`; your application owns the OTel\nSDK, exporter, collector, and provider setup.\n\nIf no OpenTelemetry SDK is configured, tracing is a no-op.\n\n## What is traced\n\nThe runtime creates spans for:\n\n- `tanstack.workflow.start_run`\n- `tanstack.workflow.deliver_signal`\n- `tanstack.workflow.deliver_approval`\n- `tanstack.workflow.sweep`\n- `tanstack.workflow.drive_run`\n\nStore calls made by the runtime are traced as child spans, such as\n`tanstack.workflow.store.claim_run`,\n`tanstack.workflow.store.append_events`, and\n`tanstack.workflow.store.claim_due_timers`.\n\nFresh `ctx.step` executions create `tanstack.workflow.step` spans. Replayed\nsteps do not create fresh step execution spans because no user step code ran.\n\n## Privacy defaults\n\nWorkflow tracing intentionally does not record workflow input, workflow output,\nsignal payloads, step results, or arbitrary step metadata as attributes.\n\nBuilt-in attributes are stable identifiers and counts:\n\n- `tanstack.workflow.workflow_id`\n- `tanstack.workflow.workflow_version`\n- `tanstack.workflow.run_id`\n- `tanstack.workflow.operation`\n- `tanstack.workflow.result_kind`\n- `tanstack.workflow.step_id`\n- `tanstack.workflow.signal_name`\n- `tanstack.workflow.schedule_id`\n- `tanstack.workflow.bucket_id`\n- `tanstack.workflow.lease_owner`\n- `tanstack.workflow.event_count`\n- `tanstack.workflow.events_truncated`\n\nIf you want to add safe application attributes, pass `telemetry.attributes` or\n`telemetry.mapStepMeta`.\n\n## Configure tracing\n\nInitialize OpenTelemetry in your app before Workflow code runs. Then create the\nruntime normally:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkflowRuntime } from '@tanstack/workflow-runtime'\n\nexport const workflowRuntime = defineWorkflowRuntime({\n  store,\n  workflows,\n})\n```\n\nWorkflow uses the global OpenTelemetry tracer provider by default.\n\nTo customize Workflow tracing:\n\n```ts\nexport const workflowRuntime = defineWorkflowRuntime({\n  store,\n  workflows,\n  telemetry: {\n    spanNamePrefix: 'tanstack.workflow',\n    attributes: ({ workflowId }) => ({\n      'app.workflow_id': workflowId ?? 'unknown',\n    }),\n    mapStepMeta: (meta) => ({\n      'app.step_name': String(meta.name),\n    }),\n  },\n})\n```\n\nOnly use `mapStepMeta` for metadata you know is safe to export. Workflow does\nnot export step metadata by default.\n\nDisable tracing for a runtime:\n\n```ts\nexport const workflowRuntime = defineWorkflowRuntime({\n  store,\n  workflows,\n  telemetry: false,\n})\n```\n\n## Deployment notes\n\nHost adapters do not need separate tracing configuration. Netlify, Vercel,\nCloudflare, and Railway helpers call `runtime.sweep()`, so they inherit the\nruntime spans automatically.\n\nFor serverless platforms, initialize the OpenTelemetry SDK in the platform's\nrecommended instrumentation entrypoint. Workflow only emits spans through the\nOpenTelemetry API; exporter flushing and process lifecycle are app concerns.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: observability\ntitle: Observability\n---\n\n# Observability\n\nTanStack Workflow emits OpenTelemetry traces from the runtime and core engine.\nThe packages depend only on `@opentelemetry/api`; your application owns the OTel\nSDK, exporter, collector, and provider setup.\n\nIf no OpenTelemetry SDK is configured, tracing is a no-op.\n\n## What is traced\n\nThe runtime creates spans for:\n\n- `tanstack.workflow.start_run`\n- `tanstack.workflow.deliver_signal`\n- `tanstack.workflow.deliver_approval`\n- `tanstack.workflow.sweep`\n- `tanstack.workflow.drive_run`\n\nStore calls made by the runtime are traced as child spans, such as\n`tanstack.workflow.store.claim_run`,\n`tanstack.workflow.store.append_events`, and\n`tanstack.workflow.store.claim_due_timers`.\n\nFresh `ctx.step` executions create `tanstack.workflow.step` spans. Replayed\nsteps do not create fresh step execution spans because no user step code ran.\n\n## Privacy defaults\n\nWorkflow tracing intentionally does not record workflow input, workflow output,\nsignal payloads, step results, or arbitrary step metadata as attributes.\n\nBuilt-in attributes are stable identifiers and counts:\n\n- `tanstack.workflow.workflow_id`\n- `tanstack.workflow.workflow_version`\n- `tanstack.workflow.run_id`\n- `tanstack.workflow.operation`\n- `tanstack.workflow.result_kind`\n- `tanstack.workflow.step_id`\n- `tanstack.workflow.signal_name`\n- `tanstack.workflow.schedule_id`\n- `tanstack.workflow.bucket_id`\n- `tanstack.workflow.lease_owner`\n- `tanstack.workflow.event_count`\n- `tanstack.workflow.events_truncated`\n\nIf you want to add safe application attributes, pass `telemetry.attributes` or\n`telemetry.mapStepMeta`.\n\n## Configure tracing\n\nInitialize OpenTelemetry in your app before Workflow code runs. Then create the\nruntime normally:\n\n```ts\nimport { defineWorkflowRuntime } from '@tanstack/workflow-runtime'\n\nexport const workflowRuntime = defineWorkflowRuntime({\n  store,\n  workflows,\n})\n```\n\nWorkflow uses the global OpenTelemetry tracer provider by default.\n\nTo customize Workflow tracing:\n\n```ts\nexport const workflowRuntime = defineWorkflowRuntime({\n  store,\n  workflows,\n  telemetry: {\n    spanNamePrefix: 'tanstack.workflow',\n    attributes: ({ workflowId }) => ({\n      'app.workflow_id': workflowId ?? 'unknown',\n    }),\n    mapStepMeta: (meta) => ({\n      'app.step_name': String(meta.name),\n    }),\n  },\n})\n```\n\nOnly use `mapStepMeta` for metadata you know is safe to export. Workflow does\nnot export step metadata by default.\n\nDisable tracing for a runtime:\n\n```ts\nexport const workflowRuntime = defineWorkflowRuntime({\n  store,\n  workflows,\n  telemetry: false,\n})\n```\n\n## Deployment notes\n\nHost adapters do not need separate tracing configuration. Netlify, Vercel,\nCloudflare, and Railway helpers call `runtime.sweep()`, so they inherit the\nruntime spans automatically.\n\nFor serverless platforms, initialize the OpenTelemetry SDK in the platform's\nrecommended instrumentation entrypoint. Workflow only emits spans through the\nOpenTelemetry API; exporter flushing and process lifecycle are app concerns.\n"}
